# Frontend env files, in the order Vite applies them (later overrides
# earlier for the same key):
#
#   .env               -> loaded in every mode (kept empty, see .env)
#   .env.development    -> loaded only by `npm run dev` (committed, no secrets)
#   .env.production      -> loaded only by `npm run build` (committed, no secrets)
#   .env.local            -> gitignored, personal overrides for either mode
#   .env.[mode].local       -> gitignored, personal overrides for one mode
#
# Only variables prefixed VITE_ are exposed to frontend code (Vite's own
# rule) — never put Firebase private keys, JWT secrets, or admin passwords
# in a VITE_ variable; those belong in worker/.dev.vars (local) or
# `wrangler secret put` (production), never in a file under src/ or here.
#
# The single value the frontend needs:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL   Base URL every axios client uses (see
#                        src/utils/constants.js — the ONLY place this is
#                        read; nothing else should hardcode an API URL).
#
#     Local:      http://127.0.0.1:8787/api   (the local `wrangler dev` Worker)
#     Production: /api                        (same-origin — Worker serves
#                                               SPA + API from one deployment)
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` only if you need to override the committed
# .env.development/.env.production defaults above (e.g. a non-default local
# Worker port). Uncomment and edit:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8787/api
